  date         = {2017-11-19},
  abstract     = {Background: Microsimulation consists of a set of techniques
                  for estimating characteristics and modelling change in
                  populations of individuals. Aims: To demonstrate how
                  microsimulation can be used by demographers who want to
                  undertake population estimates and projections. Data and
                  methods: We use data from the 2011 United Kingdom (UK) Census
