  date         = {2011-09},
  abstract     = {This essay argues that work, and the socioeconomic class
                  polarities it creates, plays a fundamental role in determining
                  inequalities in the distribution of morbidity and mortality.
                  This is by means of uneven exposure to physical hazards and
                  psychosocial risks in the workplace, as well as by
                  inequalities in exclusion from the labour market and the
